  "summary_en": "Belgian federal non-binding Code of Practice (September 2016), based on the UK 2015 code, for testing driver-assistance and automated vehicles on public roads. It sets minimum conditions on testing organisations, test drivers and operators, vehicle requirements, data recording, cybersecurity and transitions between manual and automated modes.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Testing organisation bears full responsibility; a test driver is required on public roads, or an operator at up to 30 km/h in other public places.",
   "Prior risk analysis, closed-track testing and authority engagement required before public testing.",
   "Vehicles must carry data recorders logging mode, speed, steering, braking and sensor data, available to authorities after incidents.",
   "Training, alertness and licensing requirements for test drivers and operators; manual override must always be possible.",
   "Existing insurance, traffic law and data protection rules still apply; the code itself is not law."
  ],
